  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\n\nA weakening mid level short wave will move east across our region \nand a surface cold front will shift east of the area prior to\nsunrise. Light rain shower activity associated with this system\nwill taper off from the west. \n\nLow level CAA will develop behind the front today. This will lead to\nmuch cooler temperatures with highs on today only ranging from the \nmid 40s northwest to the low 50s in the southeast.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2)\nThere is still a lot of uncertainty on exactly how the southern \nstream system lifting out of the southeast U.S. will interact and \nphase with additional mid/upper level energy dropping down from our \nnorthwest midweek. Latest trends suggest more weight toward phasing\nover the Ohio Valley. Therefore, it pcpn associated with this will \nspread into our area through Thanksgiving day and likely continue \ninto Thursday night before tapering off Friday.\n\nTemperatures will remain several degrees below normal with \ndaytime highs mostly in the 40s into next weekend. Ptype will be \nprimarily rain, but depending on how strong the northern stream \nsystem is and how much cooler air will be able to be pulled down into\nthe area, can not rule out some wet snowflakes mixing in with the \nrain Thursday night.",
